entedError), and 3.15's"] [51 1 "// complex codes their \"Zf\" and \"Zd\"."] [54 17 "// queue 473: Py_UCS4's \"w\", its itemsize the array's (BufferItemsize); memoryview has no unpacking of it"] [62 1 "// BufferItemsize is the itemsize of the array's Py_buffer (queue 473: a format memoryview does not know, \"w\")."] [65 1 "// BytesLike makes an array a bytes-like object: its buffer, not copied."] [69 17 "// nil once exhausted"] [80 1 "// arrayTypecodes315 are 3.15.2's typecodes (arraymodule.c's descriptors, queue 263): its 'e' (half float), 'Zf' and 'Zd'"] [81 1 "// (complex), held as the codes e, F and D; the module's typecodes a tuple of them."] [84 1 "// arrayCodeOf is a 3.15.2 typecode's code, 0 when it names none."] [98 1 "// arrayTypecodeName is a code's typecode: \"Zf\" and \"Zd\" for the complex codes (queue 263)."] [109 1 "// arrayComplexArg is cf_setitem's and cd_setitem's PyArg_Parse \"D;array item must be complex\" (PyComplex_AsCComplex:"] [110 1 "// a value that is no number fails in PyFloat_AsDouble, \"must be real number, not T\", as 3.15.2's oracle shows)."] [135 1 "// resize is array_resize: n items; the allocation follows arraymodule.c's growth pattern (for __sizeof__),"] [136 1 "// the bytes past the old length are the caller's to fill; refused (BufferError) while the buffer is exported and the"] [137 1 "// size changes."] [171 1 "// get is the descriptor's getitem."] [199 12 "// queue 263: 3.15.2's e_getitem, cf_getitem, cd_getitem"] [206 2 "// u, w: a code point (any 32-bit value, as PyUnicode_FromOrdinal: out of range a ValueError's"] [207 2 "// territory, never reached from Python)"] [238 1 "// encode is the descriptor's setitem without the store: v's machine value, or CPython's error."] [348 12 "// queue 263: 3.15.2's e_setitem: the float as a C float, then PyFloat_Pack2"] [395 1 "// ins is ins1: v checked, then inserted before where."] [493 1 "// dataEq is PyObject_RichCompareBool(a, b, Py_EQ): identity first."] [505 1 "// dataWarn is PyErr_